               rdfs:comment "Bridging annotation, not subsumption. The OBO term is a phenotypic abnormality / nosological category, i.e. a specifically dependent continuant, whereas this class is the material pathological disorder itself. Asserting rdfs:subClassOf between them is a category error that renders both unsatisfiable, so the relation is recorded as skos:relatedMatch instead. The has-participant axiom formerly asserted here used RO_0000057, whose domain is occurrent; it now sits on WONT_0000447 as a BFO_0000051 has-part axiom, where it is type-correct."@en ;
               rdfs:label "Methicillin-resistant Staphylococcus aureus infection" ;
               skos:relatedMatch wont:WONT_0000447 .


