###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000408
wont:WONT_0000408 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf mild:MILD_120022 ;
                  ns1:IAO_0000116 "Recategorised when the causal-role groupings 'Medical condition contributing to wound formation' / 'affecting wound healing' / 'contributing to blistering wounds' were dissolved. Those classes grouped entities by what they were said to cause, which this ontology does not assert, and they mixed material disorders with dispositions and processes. Relevance to wounds is now carried by co-location axioms on the wound classes instead of by membership in a causal class."@en ,
                                  "Reparented from BFO_0000016 disposition to MILD_120022 pathological disorder. A disorder is not a disposition. What is present in the patient is an abnormal organisation of material components in and around the wound; impaired healing is what that disorder is a disorder OF, not a potential the disorder bears. The dispositional reading was a residue of the dissolved causal-role grouping, which mixed material disorders with dispositions and processes."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound healing disorder" .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000409
wont:WONT_0000409 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf ns1:GO_0008150 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound healing related physiological process"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000410
wont:WONT_0000410 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf wont:WONT_0000390 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound infection process"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000411
wont:WONT_0000411 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf wont:WONT_0000423 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound irrigation process"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000412
wont:WONT_0000412 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf ns1:DRON_00000005 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound irrigation solution" .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000413
wont:WONT_0000413 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf ns1:OMRSE_00000012 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound manager role"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000414
wont:WONT_0000414 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf mild:MILD_120021 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound development process"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000415
wont:WONT_0000415 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf ns1:BFO_0000019 ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000197 ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom ns1:NCBITaxon_9606
                                  ] ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty ns1:RO_0002559 ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom wont:WONT_0000380
                                  ] ;
                  ns1:IAO_0000115 "A quality that inheres in a patient, that is the extent of the pain that patient feels, and that is causally influenced by a wound."@en ;
                  ns1:IAO_0000116 "Retyped from BFO_0000016 disposition to BFO_0000019 quality, and the bearer moved from the wound to the patient. Wound pain is pain felt by a patient; a wound does not feel, so it cannot be the bearer. There is always some degree of pain inhering in the patient, which is what makes this a quality rather than a disposition waiting to be realized - so the IAO_0000112 note about realization in debridement or dressing change was dropped with the disposition typing, because qualities are not realized. The single qualifying value is WONT_0000474 painful, mirroring macerated under degree of maceration."@en ;
                  ns1:IAO_0000118 "Wound pain"@en ;
                  ns1:IAO_0000232 "ON MILD MODEL COMMITMENT 4. Commitment 4 forbids asserting a causal relation between ONE DISORDER AND ANOTHER, on the ground that what a disease causes cannot be separated from what it is. This axiom is outside that scope: the wound is a disorder, but the pain is a quality of the patient, not a second disorder, so no disorder-to-disorder aetiology is claimed and no co-location rewrite is needed. RO_0002559 causally influenced by was chosen over RO_0002452 has symptom and RO_0004023, both of which carry rdfs:domain OGMS_0000031 and would silently infer the OGMS disposition-based disease model that MILD rejects. RO_0002559 has no domain or range axiom, so it carries the intended content with no side effect."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "degree of wound pain"@en .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000416
wont:WONT_0000416 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf wont:WONT_0000089 ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound palpation" .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000417
wont:WONT_0000417 rdf:type owl:Class ;
                  rdfs:subClassOf ns1:BFO_0000040 ,
                                  [ rdf:type owl:Restriction ;
                                    owl:onProperty ns1:BFO_0000050 ;
                                    owl:someValuesFrom wont:WONT_0000380
                                  ] ;
                  ns1:IAO_0000116 "Structural axiom, not a definition. This class was label-only under a bare BFO_0000040, so nothing in the ontology said it had anything to do with a wound - the mereology lived only in the class name. Asserting part_of some Wound makes the name's claim checkable and is what CQ025 was failing on. No genus-differentia definition is written here; per the C6 decision the axiom is left to carry the content."@en ;
                  rdfs:label "Wound pocket" .


###  https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/WONT/WONT_0000418
